# H2 negotiated-ALPN 200 with guest bytes, production listener.
#
# Captured by driving the REAL `qqqai serve` binary (debug build of this tree)
# over real loopback TCP against the H2/SSE fixture project (qqq.toml with
# an `sse` /events route backed by the sse-event.wat guest, TLS cert with
# SAN localhost). The test client offers ALPN `h2` and speaks a hand-rolled
# H2 frame layer (preface, SETTINGS, HEADERS; connection-level frames ACKed
# like a real client), exactly as `cli_h2_events` does in
# `crates/qqq-run/tests/cli.rs`.
#
# Observed on the wire for `GET https://shop.example.com/events`:
# - TLS negotiated ALPN: h2
# - H2 HEADERS frame, stream 1: :status 200
# - H2 DATA frames, stream 1: three `data: hello` events (39 payload bytes)
# - H2 tenant refusal control: :authority evil.example.com draws 421
#
# The committed test asserting every line below is
# `production_serve_h2_tenant_sse_live` (via `assert_h2_serves_guest_events`
# and the tenant-resolve block): negotiated == Some("h2"), status ==
# Some(200), the DATA answer starts with the guest's exact first-event
# bytes and carries >= 3 `data:` events; the unmapped-authority refusal
# asserts status == Some(421) with a body naming the unmapped host (the
# `tenant-unknown-host` marker travels in the `X-QQQ-Error` header on both
# drivers — the H1 test asserts it in the raw head, the H2 client reads
# de-framed DATA, so the H2 test asserts the host-naming body instead).
# The test pins shape (exact first-event prefix + event count), not the
# full 39 bytes: a poll-loop stream has no end, so the hex dump below is a
# bounded-capture pin like the other streaming entries, while the digest
# pins the guest bytes of that capture. Re-run to reproduce; reparse the
# hex dump and rehash to verify.
#
# The DATA payload digest below equals h2-sse-3events-body in digests.txt:
# same 39 guest bytes, second capture. The ALPN/status/authority lines are
# asserted by the test, not hashed — a status string is not a digest, so it
# is recorded here as an observation with its asserting test, while the
# digest pins the guest bytes that crossed the H2 DATA frames.

### alpn (TLS negotiation)
--- utf8 ---
h2
--- hex ---
00000000  68 32

### status (H2 HEADERS :status, stream 1)
--- utf8 ---
200
--- hex ---
00000000  32 30 30

